.TH PSVectorMax 3 2025-01-20 "PsyC 0.9.5" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
\fBPSVectorMax\fR \- Compute the maximum value in vector

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/maths.h>

.I
PSFloat  
.br
\fBPSVectorMax\fR(\fIPSFloat *a\fR, \fIlong *index\fR, \fIlong length\fR, \fIPSMathOpts *opts\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compute the maximum value among values of vector \fIa\fR having length defined by \fIlength\fR.
.br
The optional pointer \fIindex\fR can be used, if not \fINULL\fR, to retrieve the index of the maximum value.
.br
The function can take advantage of the available accelerations (both hardwware and software). By default, accelerations set in \fIPSGlobalAcceleration\fR are used, if any. However, the used accelerations methods can be changed via the \fIacceleration\fR member of the optional argument \fIopts\fR.  

.SH RETURN VALUES
The maxium value in the vector \fIa\fR.

.SH SEE ALSO
psyc(1)
